      "writtenOn": "2025-02-06T16:39:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To make sure that we don\u0027t forget to add also new properties to this check, WDYT of coupling it with the \"node adding\" logic below by using a common data structure e.g.\n```\nlet mut avf_props \u003d Vec::new();\nif let Some(v) \u003d \u0026self.trusted.secretkeeper_public_key {\n    avf_props.push((c\"secretkeeper_public_key\", v.as_slice());\n}\n// ...\nlet mut untrusted_props \u003d Vec::new();\nif self.untrusted.defer_rollback_protection {\n    untrusted_props.push((c\"defer_rollback_protection\", \u0026[]);\n}\n// ...\n```\nso that you can then\n```\nif avf_props.is_empty() \u0026\u0026 untrusted_props.is_empty() {\n    return Ok(None);\n}\n```\nand also\n```\nfor (name, value) in avf_props {\n    avb.setprop(name, value)...?;\n}\n```\n(same for `untrusted_props`) and keep it all in-sync?\n\nMaybe even encapsulate that into `{Untrusted,Trusted}DeviceTreeProperties` e.g.\n```\nimpl UntrustedDeviceTreeProperties {\n    fn get_untrusted_props(\u0026self) -\u003e Vec\u003c(\u0026Cstr, \u0026[u8])\u003e { ... }\n}\n```\nalthough not sure how easy it\u0027d be to please the borrow checker?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "8955230c9de83b0a670d4a55f05eb15ca76c0f89",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
