      "message": "Done. Yea, I\u0027m not sure how much value `get_{un}trusted_props` brings in this context. It doesn\u0027t feel like that would make it any easier to prevent someone from adding a new prop but forgetting to update the implementation that populates the Vec.  To be super robust we\u0027d probably want something closer to [patchset 3](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/3473068/3), where you have some trait to implement and must define how to convert from your trat to a `(\u0026CStr, \u0026[u8])`.  But I think that might be overkill?",
